The design failed G6 as written: the two-sweep greedy residual attack recovered a complete valid equilibrium on 1 of 8 `easy` instances. I’m not treating the other gates as sufficient. The likely fix is to enlarge the product at fixed certificate size—the per-core greedy success must occur simultaneously across more shuffled cores—then rerun the same attack unchanged. If it still succeeds, this family will not ship.
