codex
Adding unused “decoy values” reduced the greedy success, but that would harden the answer format rather than the game, so I’m discarding that approach. The stronger construction instead applies a genuine affine substitution to each four-player game block, using a different scale per block. Every player then has a distinct algebraic equilibrium probability; the answer contains exactly those used polynomials and a permutation assigning them—no filler entries. This remains an exact native game transformation and makes the adversary test meaningful.
