+The paper's Proposition 4.1 gives a four-player two-action game with a
+unique fully mixed Nash equilibrium in a degree-six number field, and
+Proposition 6.6 composes copies by products.  This module takes products of
+that game, multiplies every payoff-advantage polynomial by independently
+chosen factors that are strictly positive on the probability cube, and then
+renames players and actions.  Those transformations preserve every best
