   683	  
   684	  Now the polynomials $f_1,f_2,f_3,f_4$ from Equation~\ref{eq:polys} are
   685	  \begin{align*}
   686	    f_1(x_2,x_3,x_4)&=x_2x_3x_4+2x_2x_3-2x_2-2x_3x_4+1,\\
   687	    f_2(x_1,x_3,x_4)&=3x_1x_3x_4-3x_1x_3+x_1-x_3x_4+x_3-x_4,\\
   688	    f_3(x_1,x_2,x_4)&=x_1x_4-x_1-2x_4+1,\\
   689	    f_4(x_1,x_2,x_3)&=-x_1x_2x_3+3x_1x_3-x_2x_3+x_2-1.
   690	  \end{align*}
   691	
   692	  We show using Lemma~\ref{lmm:ne-poly-cond} that if $x_i\in\s{0,1}$ for some $i$ then 
   693	  $x\notin\NE(G_4)$. There are 8 cases.
   694	
   695	  \paragraph{Case 1: $x_1=0$} then $f_2=-x_3x_4+x_3-x_4,~f_3=-2x_4+1,~f_4=-x_2x_3+x_2-1$.
   696	  If $x_4=\frac{1}{2}$ then $f_2=\frac{x_3-1}{2}$. If $x_3=1$ then $f_4=-1<0$ so $x_4=0$ -- 
   697	  a contradiction. Therefore $x_3<1$ so $f_2<0$ so $x_2=0$. Since $x_4=\frac{1}{2}$ we get
   698	  $0=f_4=-1$ -- a contradiction.
   699	
   700	  Therefore $x_4\ne\frac{1}{2}$. If $x_4<\frac{1}{2}$ then $f_3>0$ so $x_3=1$ so $f_4=-1$ 
   701	  so $x_4=0$ so $f_2=1$ so $x_2=1$. Therefore $x=(0,1,1,0)\notin\PNE(G_4)$. If 
   702	  $x_4>\frac{1}{2}$ then $f_3<0$ so $x_3=0$ so $f_2=-x_4<0$ so $x_2=0$ so $f_4=-1$ so 
   703	  $x_4=0$ -- a contradiction.
   704	
   705	  Overall $x_4$ cannot take any value in $[0,1]$, so $x\notin\NE(G_4)$.
   706	
   707	  \paragraph{Case 2: $x_1=1$} then 
   708	  $f_2=2x_3x_4-2x_3-x_4+1,~f_3=-x_4,~f_4=-2x_2x_3+x_2+3x_3-1$.
   709	  If $x_4>0$ then $f_3<0$ so $x_3=0$ so $f_2=-x_4+1$ and $f_4=x_2-1$. If $x_4<1$ then 
   710	  $f_2>0$ so $x_2=1$ so $f_1=-1$ so $x_1=0$ -- a contradiction. Therefore, still assuming 
   711	  that $x_4>0$ we get $x_4=1$ so $f_4=x_2-1\ge0$ so $x_2=1$ so $f_1=-1$ so $x_1=0$ -- a 
   712	  contradiction.
   713	
   714	  Therefore $x_4=0$. So $f_2=-2x_3+1$. If $x_3=\frac{1}{2}$ then $f_4=\frac{1}{2}$ so 
   715	  $x_4=1$ -- a contradiction. Therefore $x_3\ne\frac{1}{2}$. If $x_3>\frac{1}{2}$ then 
   716	  $f_2<0$ so $x_2=0$ so $f_4=3x_3-1>0$ so $x_4=1$ -- a contradiction. Therefore 
   717	  $x_3<\frac{1}{2}$. Then $f_2>0$ so $x_2=1$ so $f_1=2x_3-1<0$ so $x_1=0$ -- a 
   718	  contradiction.
   719	
   720	  Overall $x_1\ne1$.

