   940	  We show using Lemma~\ref{lmm:ne-poly-cond} that if $x_i\in\s{0,1}$ for some $i$ then 
   941	  $x\notin\NE(G_5)$. The proof proceeds as follows. For each $i$ in turn, we fix $x_i \in \{ 0, 1 \}$ and consider the subgame between the 4 players obtained by restricting player $i$ to play the pure action corresponding to $x_i$. We then perform a case analysis to find all profiles $x_{-i}$ for these 4 players which are NEs in this subgame. The case analysis is similar to the case analysis in the proof of Proposition~\ref{prop:n=4}. We then show that for each such NE profile $x_{-i}$, $(2x_i-1)f_i(x_{-i})<0$, meaning~$i$ is not playing a best response to $x_{-i}$ in the full $5$-player game $G_5$. So for player $i$ to play a best response in any NE of the full $5$-player game player, $i$ will need to choose $x_i\in(0,1)$.
