133237:This is not Track A: the paper itself uses Mathematica Gröbner bases and exact root isolation. The successful distribution-specific reference algorithm strips every possible positive linear mask, decomposes the result into four-player components, and tries 11 scales and all `4!·2^4=384` player/action relabellings per scale. Its measured shipping cost was 291,178 exact coefficient probes and 1.132 s (`O(nT+4224n)` for `T` displayed terms), and it solved 8/8 as expected. Once the structural decomposition is seen, one core certificate is reused and only affine/relabel bookkeeping remains; the measured intended route is 108 exact operations. Proposition 3.2 identifies an easy regime deliberately excluded here: every three-player `2×2×2` integer-payoff game has an equilibrium expressible using rationals and square roots.
133313:From the repository root, emit instances with `bash scripts/emit.sh 2507.09422 20`. Once OpenRouter quota is available, rerun `python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2507_09422.py` here, run structural/placebo copies in separate scratch directories, copy their transcripts back, update `G9_ORACLE_RESULTS`, and regenerate `selftest_report.json`.
133317:The public affine codebook intentionally makes this a structure-recognition benchmark, not a test of discovering the paper's degree-six probabilities from scratch. Any solver that factors the positive masks and recognizes the four-player template will solve it efficiently; that successful algorithm is disclosed above. The 0/200,000 estimate is only for uniform codebook subsets and assignment permutations, not for a learned solver prior. Generic Gröbner or SMT software was not run because the module must remain standard-library-only; the exact distribution-specific factor/matching algorithm is the stronger relevant reference for these planted transformations. `canonical_key` uses the construction's role/scale incidence metadata and canonicalizes block permutations; it is not a general game-isomorphism solver. Most importantly, no four-vendor LLM hardness claim exists yet because of the exhausted external key.
