codex
Implemented a native Track B generator based on the paper’s four-player algebraic Nash equilibrium and product construction ([paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2507.09422)).

Key results:

- All deterministic gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability ≈ `1.02e-23`.
- Four heuristic attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, at most 307,436 probes and 1.239 seconds per instance.
- Intended structural route: 156 exact operations.
- A coefficient-fingerprint vulnerability in the earlier construction was found and fixed with independent dense positive masks.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.09422/gen_2507_09422.py:1)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.09422/selftest_report.json:1)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.09422/README.md:1)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.09422/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.09422/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2507.09422/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl:1)

The sole incomplete requirement is external LLM hardening. Every OpenRouter redraw returned HTTP 403 “total key limit exceeded,” so the transcripts are valid error diagnostics but provide no `hardened` verdict. A funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required before submission.
